 0, Entry Helix radius 1.
 
+**Pass starts at** (Passes tab) sets where each level starts:
+
+- **Auto** cuts the rings from the middle of the area outward. This is
+  the order that 2D Offset always cut.
+- **Outside** starts at the outer edge of the area and works in. With an
+  Outside containment, the outer edge is the stock edge: the tool starts
+  outside the stock, cuts one stepover at a time and ends on the part
+  wall. Use it to stop full-width slots in the stock.
+- **Inside** starts at the part or island wall and works out.
+
 **Do not touch** (Geometry tab, **Boundaries**): pick faces or edge chains
 to protect from every cut, plunge, ramp, helix, keep-down and rapid link
 across the full tool assembly (flutes, shank and holder). **Clearance**

From e87ba36e4db4fa7691e7facdc9753dd544bb05f3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 03:28:33 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] fix(2d): Pass starts at (Auto/Inside/Outside) for 2D
 Adaptive

2D Adaptive takes the shared pass_start field of #3316: same type,
project key, Passes-tab row and MCP door. Auto keeps every earlier
path byte for byte.

Outside cuts each piece from the air past the stock edge (the #1950
air plan); a piece with no air side makes the Offset rings cut the
area from its outer edge in, named in the notes. Inside grows from the
core of a pocket without holes (the growth plan); an area with holes
is cut by Offset rings from the hole wall out, named. The Trochoidal
method refuses Inside and Outside by name (command door, generator,
consequence line).

Stacked on #3353.

Fixes #3355

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
